# Docs prose

Applies to all user-facing copy in scope: page intros, section leads, guideline bullets, metadata descriptions, homepage blurbs, and demo labels. Write once to this standard. Do not leave choppy drafts and patch one page later.

## Rules

- Do not use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`). Prefer a period and a new sentence, or a colon when introducing a list or clarification.
- Use commas only when grammar requires them (lists of three or more, or to prevent misreading). Prefer shorter sentences over comma-heavy clauses.
- Prefer short sentences that scan easily. Cut filler.
- Do not write staccato prose. Related ideas belong in one sentence, or in a colon-led list. Never stack several one-clause sentences that all describe the same thing. Two sentences are fine when they carry distinct thoughts.
- Keep empty-value placeholders in props tables as `—` (UI convention, not prose).

## Staccato check

Before shipping copy, read it aloud. If it sounds like a telegram (period, period, period), combine related clauses.

```text
❌ An input that suggests options as you type. Keep free-form text in the field. Suggestions stay optional.
✅ An input that suggests options as you type while keeping free-form text in the field. Suggestions stay optional.

❌ mode maps to aria-autocomplete. list filters only. both filters and fills the input. inline fills without filtering. none does neither.
✅ mode maps to aria-autocomplete: list filters only, both filters and fills the input, inline fills without filtering, and none does neither.

❌ Alert Dialog component for amvn.ui. A modal confirmation dialog that interrupts the user. Built with Base UI and Tailwind CSS.
✅ Alert Dialog for amvn.ui: a modal confirmation dialog that interrupts until the user confirms or cancels, built with Base UI and Tailwind CSS.

✅ Compose a decorative icon beside the title when the action needs a stronger visual cue. Keep severity in the title text and hide the icon from assistive tech.
```

The last example is fine: two sentences, two distinct jobs.
